[{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-4774"
  :itonami.blueprint/name "Retail Sale of Second-Hand Goods (peer-to-peer/consignment resale marketplace)"
  :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "4774"
  :itonami.blueprint/isic-citation "ISIC Rev.4 4774: \"retail sale of second-hand goods\" (https://unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ/Detail/EN/27/4774)"
  :itonami.blueprint/domain :retail/secondhand-resale
  :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
  :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:consumer-protection :counterfeit-prevention :stolen-goods-reporting :circular-economy]
  :itonami.blueprint/governor :resale-governor
  :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
  :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
  :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
  :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
  :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
  "ResaleAdvisor-LLM ⊣ ResaleGovernor (resale.policy, six HARD checks: rbac ·
  stolen-goods-reporting-gate · source-provenance-gate · counterfeit-flag-gate ·
  condition-misrepresentation-gate · licensed-disclosure, plus three SOFT
  checks: confidence-floor · high-value-holding-period · dispute-always-
  escalates), a genuinely compiled langgraph-clj StateGraph
  (resale.operation/build: :intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+->
  :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold, `interrupt-before
  #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for real human-in-the-loop
  resume), append-only audit ledger (resale.store/ledger + append-ledger!,
  MemStore/DatomicStore parity). Five governed ops
  (:item/intake, :item/authenticate, :sale/confirm, :correction/request,
  :disclosure/query), each routed through the ResaleGovernor with no
  bypass. stolen-goods-reporting-gate and counterfeit-flag-gate are
  secondhand-resale-specific HARD checks with no analog in sibling
  cloud-itonami actors, modeled on real secondhand-dealer reporting
  statutes (California Business and Professions Code Section 21625 et
  seq.; New York General Business Law Article 5 Sections 60-70) --
  confidence-independent rejection of a high-value/flagged-category
  intake from a non-KYC or previously-flagged seller, and of a sale in an
  authentication-required category whose current verdict is not
  :authentic. A rollout phase gate (resale.phase) sits on top of the
  governor and can only narrow, never widen, what the governor already
  allowed. Authentication provenance is structurally scoped to one real
  free public source (resale.facts: USPTO TESS trademark search, for
  brand-registration lookup only) plus two licensed provenance classes
  (:licensed-authentication-service, :licensed-secondhand-reporting-feed)
  gated on an ACTIVE operator-registered license -- no bare 'the LLM
  inferred it' authentication verdict is accepted. The schema has no
  field anywhere for buyer payment credentials or seller bank details
  (ADR-2607113000 Section 1) -- this actor mediates listing/
  authentication/sale decisions only. 37 tests / 138 assertions green
  (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors, `clojure -M:dev:run` demo
  runnable end-to-end (8-operation walkthrough producing real commit/hold
  ledger entries for every gate)."
  :db/id -1}]
